    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive core, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (75.72) and **Junior Caminero** (74.26). **Yordan Alvarez** remains the focal point of the lineup, boasting an elite 0.460 xwOBA that justifies his start despite a neutral park factor against Ginn. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** benefits from the highest park-factor boost in the squad (+16%), making him an elite play against the vulnerable Rogers. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused utility, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.54) and **Trea Turner** (67.34) providing high-floor, high-upside scoring; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically benefits from a massive +14% platoon adjustment, positioning him as the primary engine for our stolen base pursuit in a favorable matchup against Hancock.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Gary Sanchez**, who sat just below our floor at 38.24. While his platoon advantage against Sale usually warrants consideration, the combined weight of Sale\u2019s elite 2.83 xERA and a poor historical BvP track record (35 PA) pushed him to the pine to preserve our daily game caps. Elsewhere, we are cautious regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (41.77) and **Carson Benge** (47.96); both occupy the lower rungs of our active lineup due to tough SP matchups against Schlittler and Burke respectively. While **Kazuma Okamoto** is struggling against the R/R platoon projection, his presence is necessary to maintain depth, but he will be on a short leash if his efficiency dips further during the early innings. With **Colt Keith**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** all confirmed as out of their respective lineups, our depth will be tested, leaving **Caleb Durbin** (54.71) to provide the necessary stability in the UTIL slot against the stout arm of Webb.",
